From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Finn Freas <finn.freas@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:37:48 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] placer: calibrated delay model and anchored start for the
 static placer

- xilinx: -o static-delay=C,Y1,Y2,X1,X2 (ps): the static placer's delay
  estimate C + Y1*min(dy,6) + Y2*max(dy-6,0) + X1*min(dx,12) + X2*max(dx-12,0)
  instead of the fixed 500/48/24/24/12 formula; -o static-delay=matrix uses
  the chipdb's delay matrix.
- xilinx: -o predict-cal=SITE,TILE,ALPHA,BETA: predictDelay for a LUT input
  from the same slice, another slice of the same tile, and between tiles
  (ALPHA + BETA * delay matrix).
- --placer-static-anchor-init N: an anchored start for the static placer.
- --placer-static-timing-every N, --placer-static-arc-ratio R,
  --placer-static-arc-exp E (timing-arc term),
  --placer-static-weighted-precond, -o static-grad-y, -o static-hpwl-y.

The values were fitted against Vivado's routed delay on identical
implementations. Every option is off by default and an unset option
changes nothing (.frames identical on rv_soc, bram and rv_big, 3 seeds).
